! ipl_boot.strap -- the smallest program that proves the machine can
! be loaded from a tape image and started, with NOTHING transcribed.
!
! THIS IS docs/boot_plan.md's M1 EXIT TEST.  Reference Manual printed
! p.126 (PDF 129), read first-hand, specifies the whole sequence:
!
!   1. "The exchange automatically stores in the control word location
!      for the channel responsible for the channel signal a fixed
!      control word with the following contents: Data word address = 4,
!      Chain flag = 1, Multiple flag = 0, Skip flag = 0, Count = 1,
!      Refill address = 4."
!   3. "The first word read from the unit is stored in the special core
!      storage location referred to by means of address 4.  Since the
!      fixed control word is then exhausted, its refill address causes
!      the next control word to be fetched from location 4.  Location 4
!      at this time should contain another control word specifying the
!      address at which the word immediately following should be
!      stored, and the number of words to be read from the unit."
!   5. "The computer, upon receipt of the initial-start signal, fetches
!      and executes the instruction in the location specified by the
!      data word address field of the control word in core storage
!      location 4."
!
! So: strap/mktape.py puts a control word in front of this program,
! the hardware reads that ONE word, chains to it, and it reads the
! rest.  Nothing here is pre-loaded into core by the harness -- see
! gen_ipl_tb.py.  If the tape path does not work, core storage stays
! zero and every check below reads 0.
!
! THE FIRST INSTRUCTION IS "BD" BECAUSE THE MANUAL REQUIRES IT.
! p.126: "the first instruction of a program loaded by means of the
! initial program loading technique must be BRANCH DISABLED.  This
! instruction replaces the contents of the instruction counter and
! insures that the system does not return to the enabled state."
! MCP's own bootstrap obeys the same rule -- printed p.2 line 24 is
! "X IPL BS  BD,X BEGIN  -DISABLE AND START IPL" -- so this program is
! shaped like the real one even though it is three instructions long.
!
! THE HALT IS "B,$" AND NOT THE HOUSE "BEW,$": BEW would enable the
! interruption system, which the BD above has just deliberately
! disabled, and p.126's whole point is that IPL leaves it disabled.
! Same reasoning as interval_timer_steps.strap's halt.
!
! IT MUST FIT IN SIXTEEN WORDS.  StretchIO's TapeWords is 16 and the
! control word mktape.py prepends takes one of them, so the program
! has fifteen.  Widening that is docs/boot_plan.md M0 step 2 and is
! NOT needed to reach this milestone -- which is why this milestone
! comes first.

        SLC, (8)100.0      ! load somewhere clear of the low-core
                            ! special assignments (p.111) -- in
                            ! particular clear of word 4, which the
                            ! IPL control word itself occupies
IPLBS   BD,  GO            ! p.126: the first instruction MUST be this
GO      LVI, $X1, 1234     ! prove the loaded code actually executed
        SX,  $X1, RESULT   ! ... and left a value behind
HALT    B,   $             ! halt, still disabled
RESULT  DD(BU,64), 0
        END, IPLBS
